{
  "id": "80582",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Calculating Ka and Kb from Equilibrium Concentrations (CyberLearn)",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "___selfClosing___": true,
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "qkdyptaljs3aojs",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "zxxsvhn6510i7a8",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "strong": true,
                "text": "Made this its own page - in previous version it is a section on the previous page. But don't think I need to change anything on this page. "
              }
            ],
            "id": "9rvp8vq0hz5772g",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Just as we did previously for "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "text": ", we can calculate "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "sub": true,
                "text": "a"
              },
              {
                "text": " and "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "sub": true,
                "text": "b"
              },
              {
                "text": " from equilibrium concentrations."
              }
            ],
            "id": "uh342lz8jtr60pb",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "701077718",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Acetic acid is the principal ingredient in vinegar; that's why it tastes sour. At equilibrium, a solution contains [CH"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "CO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "H] = 0.0787 M and [H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] = [CH"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "CO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] = 0.00118M. What is the value of "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "a"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " for acetic acid?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ra4c1illho36zva",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "We are asked to calculate an equilibrium constant from equilibrium concentrations. At equilibrium, the value of the equilibrium constant is equal to the reaction quotient for the reaction:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "tkkrt3i1rwexjff",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "v33fj8oeess7g5j",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ylx9y1c9r4t6hp1",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "{\\mathrm{CH}}_3{\\mathrm{CO}}_2\\mathrm H(aq)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+(aq)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm{CH}}_3{\\mathrm{CO}}_2^-(aq)",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "z86tt2xnh4tili1",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "xw335pvdw206xwb",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "K_a\\;=\\;\\frac{\\;\\lbrack{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+\\rbrack\\lbrack{\\mathrm{CH}}_3{\\mathrm{CO}}_2^-\\rbrack}{\\lbrack{\\mathrm{CH}}_3{\\mathrm{CO}}_2\\mathrm H\\rbrack}\\;=\\;\\frac{\\;(0.00118)(0.00118)}{0.0787}\\;=1.77\\times10^{-5}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              }
            ],
            "id": "2044865798",
            "selection": {
              "anchor": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  0,
                  0
                ]
              },
              "focus": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  1,
                  0
                ]
              }
            },
            "type": "content"
          }
        ],
        "id": "3599963790",
        "layout": "vertical",
        "purpose": "example",
        "type": "group"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Caffeine, C"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "8"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "10"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "N"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", is a weak base. What is the value of "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "K"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "b"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " for caffeine if a solution at equilibrium has [C"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "8"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "10"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "N"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] = 0.050 M, [C"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "8"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "10"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "N"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "4"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "H"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] = 5.0 × 10"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " M, and [OH"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] = 2.5×10"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " M?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "wi1jnzgp3cudm0z",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "At equilibrium, the value of the equilibrium constant is equal to the reaction quotient for the reaction:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "mk8t51tv4x8jw8q",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "g1d13a3ict9g3ng",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "b37o4gx6ay8fq0f",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "{\\mathrm C}_8{\\mathrm H}_{10}{\\mathrm N}_4{\\mathrm O}_2(aq)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;{\\mathrm C}_8{\\mathrm H}_{10}{\\mathrm N}_4{\\mathrm O}_2\\mathrm H^+(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm{OH}^-(aq)",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "62m4bqow4cdiz3f",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "n2u1mhmn3nigjb3",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "K_b\\;=\\frac{\\;\\lbrack\\;{\\mathrm C}_8{\\mathrm H}_{10}{\\mathrm N}_4{\\mathrm O}_2\\mathrm H^+\\rbrack\\lbrack\\mathrm{OH}^-\\rbrack}{\\lbrack{\\mathrm C}_8{\\mathrm H}_{10}{\\mathrm N}_4{\\mathrm O}_2\\rbrack}\\;=\\;\\frac{(5.0\\times10^{-3})(2.5\\times10^{-3})}{0.050}\\;=\\;2.5\\times10^{-4}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              }
            ],
            "id": "1701787242",
            "selection": {
              "anchor": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  0,
                  0
                ]
              },
              "focus": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  1,
